      "description": "Barracks Help Desk- IT - Virginia Military Institute Skip to content Calendar Offices A-Z Give Search Apply Visit Inquire Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Embrace the VMI experience – where tradition builds transformation and lifelong impact. Prospective Cadets Get started on the road to VMI and your future. Visit VMI Explore post (campus), meet cadets, and see what sets VMI apart. Appointed Students Complete required forms and prepare to arrive in August. Affording VMI Learn how generous financial aid puts a VMI education within reach. Apply Now Ready to take on the challenge? Applications open Aug. 1 each year. Information for Parents Tools and resources on how parents can assist with financial aid and support their cadets. Next Steps Upcoming Admissions Events Prepare for Success Meet the Admissions Team Enrollment Services Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit VMI Apply Now Appointed Students Affording VMI Prospective Cadets Meet the Admissions Team Prepare for Success Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Academics Academics Each program at the Institute, from engineering and the humanities, to science and business, is designed to challenge cadets academically. Academic Program VMI’s core curriculum builds the foundation for success during and after undergraduate school. Majors & Minors Rigorous courses are available in STEM and the humanities, all with small class sizes. Research & Enrichment Providing scholars with opportunities to take their learning beyond the classroom. Excellence & Achievement Nurturing top academic talent through an honors program and prestigious scholarships. Academics & Opportunities Academic Departments Summer Programs Global Education Student Support & Resources Support Services Registrar Academic Catalog Academics Academics Academic Program Academic Departments Majors & Minors Excellence & Achievement Research & Enrichment Support Services ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life The unique military aspect of a VMI cadetship prepares the next generation of leaders to serve with discipline, honor, and integrity. ROTC at VMI VMI is among the very few colleges that offer ROTC options in Army, Navy, Marine Corps, Air Force, and Space Force. Naval ROTC The Naval ROTC Unit provides two programs in which cadets may enroll: US Navy or US Marine Corps. Other Ways to Serve Cadets can prepare for other roles in government, intelligence, cyber defense, and public safety, both at the state and federal level. Army ROTC VMI boasts the largest ROTC program in the country and an award-winning Ranger Challenge Team. Air Force ROTC The Air Force ROTC program prepares cadets for service in the U.S. Air Force or U.S. Space Force air, space, and cyberspace domains. Corps Military Experience From the very first day of post, the Corps of Cadets is guided in a military lifestyle and code of conduct. Scholarships & Opportunities Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Coast Guard AUP Training & Cadet Experiences Ranger Challenge Corps of Cadets Parades Wearing the Uniform ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life ROTC at VMI Army ROTC Naval ROTC Air Force ROTC Coast Guard AUP Corps Military Experience Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Ranger Challenge Team Parades Wearing the Uniform Military Mission Stories Life On Post Life On Post Post — what most colleges call a campus — is filled with the sights and sounds of not only the Corps of Cadets, but the employees, families, and communities who support them. Annual Events & Traditions Celebrate success and witness the bonds of brotherhood unique to VMI. Center for Leadership and Ethics Programming & initiatives focused on empowering leaders to think critically, solve problems, & make ethical decisions. Post Facilities VMI boasts spaces unique to the No Ordinary College experience at the nation’s oldest state-supported military college. Ca