      "title": "VMI Holds Job Fair",
      "description": "VMI Holds Job Fair - Virginia Military Institute Skip to content Calendar Offices A-Z Give Search Apply Visit Inquire Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Embrace the VMI experience – where tradition builds transformation and lifelong impact. Prospective Cadets Get started on the road to VMI and your future. Visit VMI Explore post (campus), meet cadets, and see what sets VMI apart. Appointed Students Complete required forms and prepare to arrive in August. Affording VMI Learn how generous financial aid puts a VMI education within reach. Apply Now Ready to take on the challenge? Applications open Aug. 1 each year. Information for Parents Tools and resources on how parents can assist with financial aid and support their cadets. Next Steps Upcoming Admissions Events Prepare for Success Meet the Admissions Team Enrollment Services Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit VMI Apply Now Appointed Students Affording VMI Prospective Cadets Meet the Admissions Team Prepare for Success Scholarships, Grants, and Loans Veterans Benefits Applying for Aid Academics Academics Each program at the Institute, from engineering and the humanities, to science and business, is designed to challenge cadets academically. Academic Program VMI’s core curriculum builds the foundation for success during and after undergraduate school. Majors & Minors Rigorous courses are available in STEM and the humanities, all with small class sizes. Research & Enrichment Providing scholars with opportunities to take their learning beyond the classroom. Excellence & Achievement Nurturing top academic talent through an honors program and prestigious scholarships. Academics & Opportunities Academic Departments Summer Programs Global Education Student Support & Resources Support Services Registrar Academic Catalog Academics Academics Academic Program Academic Departments Majors & Minors Excellence & Achievement Research & Enrichment Support Services ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life The unique military aspect of a VMI cadetship prepares the next generation of leaders to serve with discipline, honor, and integrity. ROTC at VMI VMI is among the very few colleges that offer ROTC options in Army, Navy, Marine Corps, Air Force, and Space Force. Naval ROTC The Naval ROTC Unit provides two programs in which cadets may enroll: US Navy or US Marine Corps. Other Ways to Serve Cadets can prepare for other roles in government, intelligence, cyber defense, and public safety, both at the state and federal level. Army ROTC VMI boasts the largest ROTC program in the country and an award-winning Ranger Challenge Team. Air Force ROTC The Air Force ROTC program prepares cadets for service in the U.S. Air Force or U.S. Space Force air, space, and cyberspace domains. Corps Military Experience From the very first day of post, the Corps of Cadets is guided in a military lifestyle and code of conduct. Scholarships & Opportunities Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Coast Guard AUP Training & Cadet Experiences Ranger Challenge Corps of Cadets Parades Wearing the Uniform ROTC & Military Life ROTC & Military Life ROTC at VMI Army ROTC Naval ROTC Air Force ROTC Coast Guard AUP Corps Military Experience Call to Duty Scholarships Veterans Benefits Ranger Challenge Team Parades Wearing the Uniform Military Mission Stories Life On Post Life On Post Post — what most colleges call a campus — is filled with the sights and sounds of not only the Corps of Cadets, but the employees, families, and communities who support them. Annual Events & Traditions Celebrate success and witness the bonds of brotherhood unique to VMI. Center for Leadership and Ethics Programming & initiatives focused on empowering leaders to think critically, solve problems, & make ethical decisions. Post Facilities VMI boasts spaces unique to the No Ordinary College experience at the nation’s oldest state-supported military college. Cadet Life Balancing academic, military, and athletic activities to build discipline, structure, and clarity. Support & Resources Providing a safe, secure, and welcoming environment for all cadets, employees, and visitors to post. For Employees Support for departments as they contribute to the success and growth of the Corps of Cadets. Cadet Experience Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Community & Connection Calendar of Events Conferences Community VMI Alumni Life On Post Life On Post Annual Events & Traditions Cadet Life Your First Year at VMI Daily Life Clubs and Activities Center for Leadership and Ethics Support and Resources VMI Event Calendar Conferences For the Community For Employees Post Facilities Research Research Cadets, faculty, staff, and community members can find a host of resources and opportunities to delve into research topics here on post. Preston Library Explore collections including over 300,000 volumes of materials, over 5,000 non-print items, and more than 300 scientific, literary, and general interest periodicals. Museums and Archives Delve into the story of VMI and Virginia through three unique museums and a fine art collection. Institutional Review Board Guidance and oversight for research conducted by cadets, faculty, and visiting researchers in regard to human subjects. VMI Archives A wealth of primary source collections of interest to both scholars and the general public. Undergraduate Research Supporting cadets as they take their learning beyond the classroom. Sponsored Programs Providing support to faculty for research, instructional, developmental, or service projects. Museums & Digital Resources VMI Museum Virginia Museum of the Civil War Jackson House Museum Archives Digital Collections Research Highlights Cadet Research News Faculty Research & Publication News Research Research at VMI Preston Library Museums and Archives Undergraduate Research Institutional Review Board Cadet Research News Athletics Athletics VMI fields 18 NCAA Division 1 teams and a thriving club sports program, allowing every cadet an opportunity to compete and win. Let's Go Keydets News, rosters, and schedules for NCAA teams at home and on the road. Support Our Keydets Go Big Red! Providing opportunity while increasing competitiveness in NCAA Athletics. Play-by-Play Get an inside look at cadet-athletes and their experiences on and off the field. Game Day Info Plan ahead for a day on post during home football games in Foster Stadium. Schedules & Tickets Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Zone Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store Athletics at VMI Athletics at VMI Let's Go Keydets Play-by-Play Support Our Keydets Game Day Athletics Calendar Football & Basketball Tickets Fan Gear at the VMI Bookstore Athletics Social Media VMI NIL Store VMI Stories About VMI About VMI Dedicated to developing leaders grounded in discipline, honor, and service since 1839. Institute Leadership Honoring tradition and providing leadership, support, and guidance to the Corps of Cadets. Historic Post Located in the beautiful Shenandoah Valley, our grounds are recognized as a national historic district. VMI Webcam Streams Get a look at daytime scenes on post with views from Smith Hall and Preston Library. No Ordinary College Continuing to lead as a top-choice for undergraduate education with strong return on investment and commitment to affordability. A Culture of Excellence Producing educated and honorable citizen-leaders who excel in all aspects of the VMI experience. Quick Links History & Legacy Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan Job Openings at VMI VMI Org Chart About VMI About VMI Institute Leadership No Ordinary College A Culture of Excellence Our Location History & Legacy VMI Webcam Streams Regulations and Policies Offices A-Z Strategic Plan VMI Org Chart Calendar Offices A-Z Give Search Apply Visit Inquire VMI Stories Institute News VMI Holds Job Fair July 12, 2023 Share The human resources office at Virginia Military Institute will hold a job fair for non-faculty positions Thursday, July 20 from 9 a.m. – 4 p.m. at the Corps Physical Training Facility located at 329 North Main Street in Lexington. Jobs available include infirmary RN, computer support technician, custodians, facility manager and technologist for the Center for Leadership and Ethics, information security officer, tailors, and more. Applicants should bring their resumes and be prepared for an interview. Hiring on-site is possible. Some positions would be pending a background check. For more information, contact human resources at 540-464-7322 or at hroffice@vmi.edu . A full list of open positions at VMI is also available on the VMI website. -VMI- Related News Mount Vernon Historian Speaks at VMI Convocation VMI Featured in TIME’s Inaugural College Rankings Cadet-Athletes Build Playset for Local Cancer Patient Record Number New Cadets Arrive to VMI Meet the 187th Regimental Leadership Institute Report The Institute Report, VMI's monthly newsletter, offers news and features on cadet, faculty, and staff activities on and off post and is published eight times each academic year. Download the Latest Report The Latest Institute News Institute News Mount Vernon Historian Speaks at VMI Convocation Institute News Cadet-Athletes Build Playset for Local Cancer Patient Institute News Record Number New Cadets Arrive to VMI Institute News Meet the 187th Regimental Leadership Institute News Cadet Spotlight Research & Innovation Military Mission Athletic News Alumni In Focus Post Announcements VMI in the News Lexington, Virginia 24450 (540) 464-7230 admissions@vmi.edu Future Cadets Admissions Financial Aid Majors & Minors Academic Support Cadet Life ROTC at VMI Keydets Athletics Cadets & Community News from Post Calendar of Events Health, Wellness, & Safety Preston Library Museums and Archives VMI Social Media Alumni Agencies Information Location Offices A-Z Jobs at VMI Student Consumer Information Regulations and Policies Freedom of Information Act Inspector General & Title IX © Virginia Military Institute | Technical questions? Contact VMI Digital Communications | Web Privacy Policy Looking for the Portal, Post View, or Proxy Pay Access? Visit & Bookmark MyVMI"
